abstract: >-
  A first-principles theoretical formulation and 40-suite numerical
  verification benchmark exploring whether the Standard Model of physics (hbar, c,
  SU(3)_C x SU(2)_L x U(1)_Y, and a single hadronic scale anchor M_N = 938.9187 MeV
  locked to the UV Planck-sphere saturation mass M_UV) can account for gravitational,
  cosmological, and subatomic observations without postulating classical/quantum
  spin-2 gravity (G_bare = 0), Dark Matter, Dark Energy (Lambda = 0), scalar inflatons,
  or Peccei-Quinn axions, modeling these effects via an Effective Uncertainty Field
  propagating at the speed of light c. Enforces 16 programmatic Referee Gates across
  85 causal factors (F0-F81) and 1,011 directed edges with zero free dimensionless
  parameters and zero numerology.
